================================================================================
Third-party frameworks, taxonomies and standards
================================================================================

This project maps generated threats to public security frameworks so that its
output is traceable. Understanding exactly what is redistributed matters, so it
is stated plainly:

WHAT IS REDISTRIBUTED
  Identifiers and short official names only -- for example "CWE-287",
  "CAPEC-151", "V2.2.1", "PR.AA-01", "A.8.24", "LLM01:2025", "AML.T0051".
  These are used as references, the way a bibliography cites a work.

WHAT IS NOT REDISTRIBUTED
  The normative text of any standard. No control descriptions, requirement
  text, questionnaire items or guidance are copied from the sources below. All
  descriptive prose shipped in this repository -- including every `notes` field
  in the framework map files and every heuristic description -- was written for
  this project.

WHAT THIS MEANS FOR YOU
  A mapping here is a pointer for traceability. It is not a certified
  crosswalk, it is not endorsed by any of the organisations below, and it does
  not by itself demonstrate compliance with anything. Read the source.

